    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Germany:\nFebruary 2I, 1970\nDear Debby:\nI have been travelling so much in connection with aviation\nand conservation activities that my mail has been terribly\nneglected - letters stacked high and unopened -- five trips\naround the world last year in addition to I don't know how\nmany to Europe and the west coast, etc. This is my second\ntrip to Europe within two weeks.\nAll in excuse for not writing\nto you much sooner.\nI don't keep a permanent secretary, and\ntemporary help is of little value to me in the kind of life I\nI must be in Hawaii (Pan American) the first week of March.\nThen, by the end of the week, in New York. Then the Philippines;\nJapan; then Europe again. I'd like very much to help with\nconservation activities on Captiva and Sanibel, but I don't see\nhow I can get to Florida in the near future. Anyway, I think\nthat to be effective the first steps must be taken by local\norganization rather than anything I could do by flying down\nthere now. I suggest the following:\nThe Nature Conservancy is.\nto assist wire conservation 288it/ll ayou are apparentay\nencountering on Captiva and Sanibel. The NC has assisted with\nliterally hundreds of conservation projects all over\nthe country,\nand can give far better advice as to procedure than I can.\npresident is an extraordinarily able man, certainly one of the\nbest in the field.\n(Last year, Anne gave a small island she\nowned in Maine to the Nature Conservancy to include with its\nMaine-coast-island project.)\nI suggest that you write to Mr. Richards, the NC president,\nfor advice about procedures on Captiva and Sanibel. Don't\nhesitate to say that I suggested this if you wish to. I expect\nto see tir. Richards soon after I return to the United States,\nand will also talk to him about it. I agree fully that it would\nbe a tragedy to have those wonderful islands spoiled through\nexcessive development.\nMr. Thomas W. Richards\nPresident\nNature Conservancy\nI522 K Street, N.W.\nwashington, D.C.\n20005\nThanks a great deal lor the invitation to visit. Anne and\nI would love to see you, and also to come to Captiva again. I\nwish I could say we would hop on a plane and come right down; but\nthat is simply impossible for me at this time.\nBest to you always, in which I know Anne joins me,\nChand",
      "Deutsche Bundespost\nerg\nSOEST/ WESTFALEN\nVIA AIR MAIL\nCORREO AEREO\nMrs. Harold M. Bixby\nCaptiva Island\nFlorida 33924\nU SA\nPAR\nAVION"
    ],
